From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:50:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] home: a macro tile's label follows the screen's language

The Kiln home layout names its unload tile with "label": "Unload"
(patch 0011). The tile drew a label with lv_label_set_text(), with no
translation lookup, so it read "Unload" in every language, although
every catalog has the word and the tile's sizing already measured its
translation (issue #23).

A set label is now the name label's translation tag: it shows in the
screen's language and follows a language change by itself. LVGL keeps
its own copy of the tag. A label that no catalog has shows as written.
A tile without a label shows the macro's own name, not translated, as
before.

Tests: the tile in a test language, a label without a translation and a
macro's own name; and every label in the AD5X home seed is a key in
each translations/*.yml.
---
diff --git a/src/ui/widgets/favorite_macro_widget.cpp b/src/ui/widgets/favorite_macro_widget.cpp
index cad2324..918220b 100644
--- a/src/ui/widgets/favorite_macro_widget.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/widgets/favorite_macro_widget.cpp
@@ -193,11 +193,17 @@ void FavoriteMacroWidget::update_display() {
         if (unconfigured) {
             // A tag, not lv_tr() text: the label then re-translates itself.
             lv_label_set_translation_tag(name_label_, "Configure");
+        } else if (!label_.empty()) {
+            // A layout's label (the Kiln seed's "Unload") is a tag too: it shows
+            // in the screen's language and follows a language change. A label
+            // with no translation shows as written, as TileSizing measures it.
+            lv_label_set_translation_tag(name_label_, label_.c_str());
         } else {
-            std::string display = label_.empty()
-                                      ? helix::get_display_name(macro_name_, helix::DeviceType::MACRO)
-                                      : label_;
-            lv_label_set_text(name_label_, display.c_str());
+            // set_text drops a tag left by an earlier state. A macro's own name
+            // is not translated anywhere in the UI.
+            lv_label_set_text(
+                name_label_,
+                helix::get_display_name(macro_name_, helix::DeviceType::MACRO).c_str());
         }
     }
 
diff --git a/tests/unit/test_default_layout.cpp b/tests/unit/test_default_layout.cpp
index 70c9c1c..e0f27b1 100644
--- a/tests/unit/test_default_layout.cpp
+++ b/tests/unit/test_default_layout.cpp
@@ -3080,3 +3080,37 @@ TEST_CASE("default_layout: the ad5x seed leaves every other grid as shipped",
         CHECK(with.disabled == without.disabled);
     }
 }
+
+// A tile draws its seed label as a translation key (FavoriteMacroWidget), so
+// the label follows the screen's language only where the catalog has that
+// key. Without one the tile stays English, as Unload did.
+TEST_CASE("default_layout: the ad5x seed's tile labels are translation keys",
+          "[default_layout][shipped][ad5x][i18n]") {
+    const auto seed = load_ad5x_seed();
+    std::set<std::string> labels;
+    for (const auto& anchor : seed.at("anchors")) {
+        if (anchor.contains("config") && anchor["config"].contains("label")) {
+            labels.insert(anchor["config"]["label"].get<std::string>());
+        }
+    }
+    REQUIRE(labels.count("Unload") == 1);
+
+    // The YAML catalogs, not ui_xml/translations: the build makes the packs
+    // from them, and the tree's packs lack the languages Kiln adds.
+    int catalogs = 0;
+    for (const auto& entry : fs::directory_iterator(helix::asset_path("translations"))) {
+        if (entry.path().extension() != ".yml") {
+            continue;
+        }
+        ++catalogs;
+        std::ifstream in(entry.path());
+        const std::string yml((std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(in)),
+                              std::istreambuf_iterator<char>());
+        for (const auto& label : labels) {
+            INFO(entry.path().filename().string() << ": " << label);
+            CHECK((yml.find("\n  " + label + ": ") != std::string::npos ||
+                   yml.find("\n  '" + label + "': ") != std::string::npos));
+        }
+    }
+    CHECK(catalogs >= 11); // de en es fr it ja ko pt ru tr zh
+}
